title: Cabinet Formation
subtitle: Four steps: the cabinet, the role of PPS, the prime minister and the PPS portfolios. Every partner's score is visible before the commit.
new-page: true
is-card: true
tags: parliament_affairs
card-image: img/polish/polish_cabinet_formation.jpg
view-if: {! return !!Q.S && PolishGovernment.formationVisible(Q) !}
on-arrival: {!
// Card parliament.cabinet_formation (technical reference 8.3, 8.4, 8.7, 8.8; card catalogue 7.1; Z — 0.61).
// Four steps on one hub: changing a setting is free and returns here; the commit appoints an accepted offer at once.
// A mandatory formation costs no month; the player's own initiative costs one.
if (!Q.S) return;
var neg = PolishGovernment.enterFormation(Q);
var view = PolishGovernment.formationView(Q);
var submit = PolishGovernment.submitStatus(Q);
Q.pl_form_mandatory = view.mandatory ? 1 : 0;
Q.pl_form_post_election = view.reason === 'post_election' ? 1 : 0;
Q.pl_form_config = view.configuration;
Q.pl_form_clubs = view.clubs;
Q.pl_form_candidate = view.candidate;
Q.pl_form_candidate_note = view.candidate_note;
Q.pl_form_mode = view.mode;
Q.pl_form_minorities = view.minorities;
Q.pl_form_minority_seats = view.minority_seats;
Q.pl_form_minority_allowed = view.minority_allowed ? 1 : 0;
Q.pl_form_seek = neg.draft.seek_minority_support ? 1 : 0;
Q.pl_form_is_opposition = neg.draft.pps_mode === 'opposition' ? 1 : 0;
Q.pl_form_free_portfolios = PolishGovernment.draftPortfolioChoice(Q) ? 1 : 0;
Q.pl_form_portfolios = view.portfolios;
Q.pl_form_points = view.points;
Q.pl_form_programme = view.programme;
Q.pl_form_majority = view.majority;
Q.pl_form_votes = view.votes;
Q.pl_form_verdict = view.verdict;
Q.pl_form_submit_reason = submit.reason;
// Up to eight partners, one line each with the parts of the score (decision 1B of 0.61).
for (var i = 0; i < 8; i++) {
    Q['pl_form_p' + (i + 1)] = view.partner_lines[i] || '';
    Q['pl_form_p' + (i + 1) + '_on'] = view.partner_lines[i] ? 1 : 0;
}
// 9.7: the stabilisation terms of Grabski belong to this same card (no separate Grabski card).
Q.pl_form_terms_open = view.stabilisation_open ? 1 : 0;
Q.pl_form_terms = view.stabilisation;
Q.pl_form_terms_protections_why = PolishGovernment.stabilisationTermsStatus('protections', Q).reason;
// Stage 8 (A1): the cause of a crisis opened by a dated input of the scenario.
Q.pl_form_cause = typeof PolishPolitics !== 'undefined' && PolishPolitics.crisisNote ? PolishPolitics.crisisNote(Q) : '';
Q.pl_form_cause_on = Q.pl_form_cause ? 1 : 0;
!}

= Forming a cabinet

[? if pl_form_post_election : The certified election result opens the formation of a new cabinet. This mandatory formation costs no month. ?]

[? if pl_form_cause_on : [+ pl_form_cause +] ?]

[? if pl_form_mandatory and not pl_form_post_election : A cabinet crisis is open. The caretaker cabinet governs until a new one is appointed. This mandatory formation costs no month. ?]

[? if not pl_form_mandatory : A cabinet crisis is open. Our own initiative spends this month's action when the offer is submitted; closing the card is free. ?]

[? if not pl_form_is_opposition : **1. The cabinet:** [+ pl_form_config +] ([+ pl_form_clubs +]). Programme: [+ pl_form_programme +]. ?]

[? if pl_form_is_opposition : **1. The cabinet:** none of ours. ?]

**2. The role of PPS:** [+ pl_form_mode +]. [? if pl_form_minority_allowed and not pl_form_is_opposition : Support of the minority representations ([+ pl_form_minority_seats +] MPs): [+ pl_form_minorities +]. ?] [? if pl_form_terms_open : Terms of our toleration of Grabski: [+ pl_form_terms +]. ?]

[? if not pl_form_is_opposition : **3. The prime minister:** [+ pl_form_candidate +]. [+ pl_form_candidate_note +] ?]

[? if not pl_form_is_opposition : **4. The PPS portfolios:** [+ pl_form_portfolios +]. [+ pl_form_points +] ?]

[? if not pl_form_is_opposition : **The partners' scores.** Each club agrees at 60 or more: 30% relation with PPS, 35% programme, 20% its portfolio or demands, 15% credibility of PPS, minus broken promises. ?]

[? if pl_form_p1_on : [+ pl_form_p1 +] ?]

[? if pl_form_p2_on : [+ pl_form_p2 +] ?]

[? if pl_form_p3_on : [+ pl_form_p3 +] ?]

[? if pl_form_p4_on : [+ pl_form_p4 +] ?]

[? if pl_form_p5_on : [+ pl_form_p5 +] ?]

[? if pl_form_p6_on : [+ pl_form_p6 +] ?]

[? if pl_form_p7_on : [+ pl_form_p7 +] ?]

[? if pl_form_p8_on : [+ pl_form_p8 +] ?]

[? if not pl_form_is_opposition : **Votes:** [+ pl_form_votes +] ?]

**Result:** [+ pl_form_verdict +]

- @configurations: 1. Choose the cabinet
- @modes: 2. Change the role of PPS
- @minorities_on
- @minorities_off
- @terms_menu: 2. Set the terms of the stabilisation
- view-if: pl_form_terms_open
- @candidates: 3. Choose the prime minister
- view-if: not pl_form_is_opposition
- @portfolios
- @submit
- @easy_discard
- view-if: not pl_form_mandatory

@minorities_on
title: 2. Ask the minority representations for external support
subtitle: Their [+ pl_form_minority_seats +] MPs may vote for the cabinet. Language, school and legal-equality rights enter the agreement; minorities receive no portfolios.
view-if: pl_form_minority_allowed and not pl_form_seek and not pl_form_is_opposition
on-arrival: {!
PolishGovernment.setDraft(Q, 'seek_minority_support', true);
!}
go-to: polish_cabinet_formation

@minorities_off
title: 2. Do not ask the minority representations for support
view-if: pl_form_seek and not pl_form_is_opposition
on-arrival: {!
PolishGovernment.setDraft(Q, 'seek_minority_support', false);
!}
go-to: polish_cabinet_formation

@portfolios
title: 4. Choose the PPS portfolios
subtitle: [+ pl_form_points +]
view-if: pl_form_free_portfolios
go-to: portfolio_menu

@terms_menu
new-page: true

= Terms of the stabilisation

Grabski's stabilisation profile is part of this offer (9.7). By default he stabilises quickly with named cuts and a wealth tax. Our toleration can ask for other terms; he may refuse our demands if he has enough support without us. Changing the terms is free.

- @terms_none
- @terms_loan
- @terms_protections
- @back

@terms_none
title: No terms of our own
subtitle: Grabski keeps his default profile.
on-arrival: {!
PolishGovernment.setDraft(Q, 'stabilisation_terms', 'none');
!}
go-to: polish_cabinet_formation

@terms_loan
title: Tolerate him for a loan and limited cuts
subtitle: The stabilisation becomes gradual and is financed by a domestic loan; no rapid cuts while PPS tolerates him.
on-arrival: {!
PolishGovernment.setDraft(Q, 'stabilisation_terms', 'loan');
!}
go-to: polish_cabinet_formation

@terms_protections
title: Tolerate him for protections and a heavier burden on wealth
subtitle: The full protection for the unemployed by the fourth month and a wealth tax to pay for it. Needs the party apparatus at level 2, a union branch with reach 40 and a relation of 40 with Grabski; he may still refuse.
choose-if: {! return PolishGovernment.stabilisationTermsStatus('protections', Q).available !}
unavailable-subtitle: [+ pl_form_terms_protections_why +]
on-arrival: {!
PolishGovernment.setDraft(Q, 'stabilisation_terms', 'protections');
!}
go-to: polish_cabinet_formation

@submit
title: Submit the offer
subtitle: [? if pl_form_mandatory : No month is spent. ?][? if not pl_form_mandatory : Spends this month's action. ?]
choose-if: {! return PolishGovernment.submitStatus(Q).available !}
unavailable-subtitle: [+ pl_form_submit_reason +]
on-arrival: {!
// The one commit: an accepted PPS offer is appointed at once; otherwise a cabinet without PPS, if any (Z — 0.61).
if (Q.S.negotiation && Q.S.negotiation.kind === 'cabinet' && Q.S.negotiation.phase === 'draft') {
    var result = PolishGovernment.submitFormation(Q);
    Q.pl_form_return_to_election = 0;
    if (result.reason === 'post_election' && Q.sejm_pending && Q.sejm_pending.phase === 'results') {
        Q.sejm_pending.government_choice = result.appointed ? result.appointed.cabinet_id : 'no_cabinet';
        Q.pl_form_return_to_election = 1;
    }
}
var view = PolishGovernment.formationResultView(Q);
Q.pl_fres_offer = view.offer;
Q.pl_fres_forecast = view.forecast;
Q.pl_fres_answers = view.answers;
Q.pl_fres_appointed = view.appointed;
Q.pl_fres_minority = view.minority_note;
Q.pl_fres_failed = view.failed;
!}
go-to: result

@result
new-page: true

= The result

Our offer: [+ pl_fres_offer +].

[? if pl_fres_forecast : Declared votes on our offer: [+ pl_fres_forecast +]. ?]

[? if pl_fres_answers : Answers: [+ pl_fres_answers +]. ?]

[? if pl_fres_appointed : **The head of state appoints [+ pl_fres_appointed +].** ?]

[? if pl_fres_minority : [+ pl_fres_minority +] ?]

[? if pl_fres_failed : [+ pl_fres_failed +] ?]

- @done: Continue.

@done
go-to: sejm_election.finish if pl_form_return_to_election; root if not pl_form_return_to_election

@back
title: Back to the offer
go-to: polish_cabinet_formation

@configurations
new-page: true
on-arrival: {!
for (var id of PolishGovernment.PPS_CONFIGURATIONS) {
    Q['pl_cfg_' + id + '_line'] = PolishGovernment.coalitionLine(Q, id).line;
}
Q.pl_cfg_opposition_line = PolishGovernment.oppositionLine(Q);
!}

= 1. Choose the cabinet

Each line shows the clubs and their MPs, the score of each partner with PPS in the cabinet (a partner agrees at 60 or more) and the votes. A majority needs [+ pl_form_majority +] MPs; a minority cabinet needs more votes for than against. A cabinet that is not possible now is greyed with the reason. Each cabinet has a fixed minimum programme; it enters the agreement with the partners.

- @cfg_left_minority
- @cfg_centre_left
- @cfg_left_labour
- @cfg_pps_majority
- @cfg_broad_centre
- @cfg_skrzynski_broad
- @cfg_national_unity
- @cfg_united_left
- @cfg_workers_front
- @cfg_expert
- @cfg_opposition
- @back

